sequence01	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	85018	85938	.	-	0	ID=MGA_79;product=catechol 1%2C2-dioxygenase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_002113693.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_00780;gene=catA;EC_number=1.13.11.1;note=WP_002113693.1 catechol 1%2C2-dioxygenase (Acinetobacter) [pid:95.8%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:2.7e-168],Domain:cl26360:PcaH Protocatechuate 3%2C4-dioxygenase beta subunit  [Secondary metabolites biosynthesis%2C transport and catabolism]. Members of this family known so far are catechol 1%2C2-dioxygenases of the Proteobacteria. They are distinct from catechol 1%2C2-dioxygenases and chlorocatechol 1%2C2-dioxygenases of the Actinobacteria%2C which are quite similar to each other and resolved by separate models. This enzyme catalyzes intradiol cleavage in which catechol + O2 becomes cis%2Ccis-muconate. Catechol is an intermediate in the catabolism of many different aromatic compounds%2C as is the alternative intermediate protocatechuate. In Acinetobacter lwoffii%2C two isozymes are present with abilities%2C differing somewhat%2C to act on catechol analogs 3-methylcatechol%2C 4-methylcatechol%2C 4-methoxycatechol%2C and 4-chlorocatechol. [Energy metabolism%2C Other] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:92-276%2C Eval:1.8e-32%2C score:117.1],MGA_79
