sequence03	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	137143	138483	.	-	0	ID=MGA_662;product=deoxyguanosinetriphosphate triphosphohydrolase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014207388.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_06600;note=WP_014207388.1 deoxyguanosinetriphosphate triphosphohydrolase (Acinetobacter) [pid:96.6%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:6.1e-253],Domain:cl26231:YdhJ HD superfamily phosphohydrolase [General function prediction only]. dGTP triphosphohydrolase (dgt) releases inorganic triphosphate%2C an unusual activity reaction product%2C from GTP. Its activity has been called limited to the Enterobacteriaceae%2C although homologous sequences are detected elsewhere. This finding casts doubt on whether the activity is shared in other species. In several of these other species%2C the homologous gene is found in an apparent operon with dnaG%2C the DNA primase gene. The enzyme from E. coli was shown to bind coopertatively to single stranded DNA. The biological role of dgt is unknown. [Purines%2C pyrimidines%2C nucleosides%2C and nucleotides%2C Nucleotide and nucleoside interconversions] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:4-440%2C Eval:3.8e-79%2C score:248.8],MGA_662
