sequence04	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	66136	67701	.	-	0	ID=MGA_834;product=alkyl hydroperoxide reductase subunit F;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014206203.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_08310;gene=ahpF;note=WP_014206203.1 alkyl hydroperoxide reductase subunit F (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:97.1%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:98.7%25%2C Eval:4.6e-287],Domain:cl26177:Pyr_redox_2 Pyridine nucleotide-disulphide oxidoreductase. This enzyme is the partner of the peroxiredoxin (alkyl hydroperoxide reductase) AhpC which contains the peroxide-reactive cysteine. AhpF contains the reductant (NAD(P)H) binding domain (pfam00070) and presumably acts to resolve the disulfide which forms after oxidation of the active site cysteine in AphC. This proteins contains two paired conserved cysteine motifs%2C CxxCP and CxHCDGP. [Cellular processes%2C Detoxification%2C Cellular processes%2C Adaptations to atypical conditions] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-520%2C Eval:0.0e+00%2C score:833.2],MGA_834
