sequence04	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	100860	101744	.	-	0	ID=MGA_868;product=triphosphoribosyl-dephospho-CoA synthase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014206491.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_08650;EC_number=2.4.2.52;note=WP_014206491.1 triphosphoribosyl-dephospho-CoA synthase (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:94.6%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:5.3e-153],Domain:cl00768:CitG ATP:dephospho-CoA triphosphoribosyl transferase. This protein acts in cofactor biosynthesis%2C preparing the coenzyme A derivative that becomes attached to the malonate decarboxylase acyl carrier protein (or delta subunit). The closely related protein CitG of citrate lyase produces the same molecule%2C but the two families are nonetheless readily separated. [Biosynthesis of cofactors%2C prosthetic groups%2C and carriers%2C Other] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:9-288%2C Eval:2.9e-43%2C score:146.8],MGA_868
sequence04	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	101744	103423	.	-	0	ID=MGA_869;product=malonate decarboxylase subunit alpha;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014206490.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_08660;gene=mdcA;note=WP_014206490.1 malonate decarboxylase subunit alpha (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:99.3%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:0.0e+00],Domain:cl25563:Mal_decarbox_Al Malonate decarboxylase%2C alpha subunit%2C transporter. This model describes malonate decarboxylase alpha subunit%2C from both the water-soluble form as found in Klebsiella pneumoniae and the form couple to sodium ion pumping in Malonomonas rubra. Malonate decarboxylase Na+ pump is the paradigm of the family of Na+ transport decarboxylases. Essentially%2C it couples the energy derived from decarboxylation of a carboxylic acid substrate to move Na+ ion across the bilayer. Functional malonate decarboylase is a multi subunit protein. The alpha subunit enzymatically performs the transfer of malonate (substrate) to an acyl carrier protein subunit for subsequent decarboxylation%2C hence the name: acetyl-S-acyl carrier protein:malonate carrier protein-SH transferase. [Transport and binding proteins%2C Cations and iron carrying compounds%2C Energy metabolism%2C Other] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:148-220%2C Eval:8.2e-07%2C score:48.5%2C C-term missing],MGA_869
