sequence04	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	237386	238675	.	+	0	ID=MGA_992;product=fosfomycin efflux MFS transporter AbaF;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014206390.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_09890;gene=abaF;note=WP_014206390.1 fosfomycin efflux MFS transporter AbaF (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:94.7%25%2C q_cov:97.2%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:7.6e-229],Domain:cl26210:MFS_2 MFS/sugar transport protein. The Glycoside-Pentoside-Hexuronide (GPH):Cation Symporter Family (TC 2.A.2) GPH:cation symporters catalyze uptake of sugars in symport with a monovalent cation (H+ or Na+). Members of this family includes transporters for melibiose%2C lactose%2C raffinose%2C glucuronides%2C pentosides and isoprimeverose. Mutants of two groups of these symporters (the melibiose permeases of enteric bacteria%2C and the lactose permease of Streptococcus thermophilus) have been isolated in which altered cation specificity is observed or in which sugar transport is uncoupled from cation symport (i.e.%2C uniport is catalyzed). The various members of the family can use Na+%2C H+ or Li%2C Na+ or Li+%2C H+ or Li+%2C or only H+ as the symported cation. All of these proteins possess twelve putative transmembrane a-helical spanners. [Transport and binding proteins%2C Carbohydrates%2C organic alcohols%2C and acids] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:149-385%2C Eval:1.9e-07%2C score:49.9%2C N-term missing],MGA_992
