sequence05	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	79816	80091	.	+	0	ID=MGA_1087;product=type II toxin-antitoxin system Phd/YefM family antitoxin;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_000213183.1;translation=MNHIIHSRFVASVSELKKNPTAVVQNAFGEAVAILNRNNPEFYCVPAAMYERMMDLIEDQELIKLAEQVDTDETVKVSINELRARVLKNSS;locus_tag=LOCUS_10840;note=WP_000213183.1 type II toxin-antitoxin system Phd/YefM family antitoxin (Vibrio) [pid:51.4%25%2C q_cov:79.1%25%2C s_cov:87.8%25%2C Eval:1.8e-15],Domain:cl09153:PhdYeFM_antitox Antitoxin Phd_YefM%2C type II toxin-antitoxin system. This model recognizes a region of about 55 amino acids toward the N-terminal end of bacterial proteins of about 85 amino acids in length. The best-characterized member is prevent-host-death (phd) of bacteriophage P1%2C the antidote partner of death-on-curing (doc) (TIGR01550) in an addiction module. Addiction modules prevent plasmid curing by killing the host cell as the longer-lived killing protein persists while the gene for the shorter-lived antidote is lost. Note%2C however%2C that relatively few members of this family appear to be plasmid or phage-encoded. Also%2C there is little overlap%2C except for phage P1 itself%2C of species with this family and with the doc family. [Cellular processes%2C Toxin production and resistance%2C Mobile and extrachromosomal element functions%2C Other] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:11-62%2C Eval:2.9e-08%2C score:43.9%2C C-term missing],MGA_1087
