sequence06	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	135357	139055	.	-	0	ID=MGA_1355;product=UvrD-helicase domain-containing protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014208244.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_13520;note=WP_014208244.1 UvrD-helicase domain-containing protein (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:91.6%25%2C q_cov:99.5%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:0.0e+00],Domain:cl28312:UvrD Superfamily I DNA or RNA helicase [Replication%2C recombination and repair]. AddAB%2C also called RexAB%2C substitutes for RecBCD in several bacterial lineages. These DNA recombination proteins act before synapse and are particularly important for DNA repair of double-stranded breaks by homologous recombination. The term AddAB is used broadly%2C with AddA homologous between the Firmicutes (as modeled here) and the alphaproteobacteria%2C while the partner AddB proteins show no strong homology across the two groups of species. [DNA metabolism%2C DNA replication%2C recombination%2C and repair] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:22-1195%2C Eval:3.6e-125%2C score:411.9],MGA_1355
