sequence06	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	143395	144813	.	-	0	ID=MGA_1358;product=polyphosphate--AMP phosphotransferase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005065911.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_13550;note=WP_005065911.1 polyphosphate--AMP phosphotransferase (Acinetobacter) [pid:97.0%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.2e-275],Domain:cl11971:PPK2 Polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2). Members of this protein family belong to the polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2) family%2C which is not related in sequence to PPK1. While PPK1 tends to act in the biosynthesis of polyphosphate%2C or poly(P)%2C members of the PPK2 family tend to use the terminal phosphate of poly(P) to regenerate ATP or GTP from the corresponding nucleoside diphosphate%2C or ADP from AMP as is the case with polyphosphate:AMP phosphotransferase (PAP). Members of this protein family most likely transfer the terminal phosphate between poly(P) and some nucleotide%2C but it is not clear which. [Central intermediary metabolism%2C Phosphorus compounds] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:247-469%2C Eval:5.4e-86%2C score:262.3],Domain:cl11971:PPK2 Polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2). Members of this protein family belong to the polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2) family%2C which is not related in sequence to PPK1. While PPK1 tends to act in the biosynthesis of polyphosphate%2C or poly(P)%2C members of the PPK2 family tend to use the terminal phosphate of poly(P) to regenerate ATP or GTP from the corresponding nucleoside diphosphate%2C or ADP from AMP as is the case with polyphosphate:AMP phosphotransferase (PAP). Members of this protein family most likely transfer the terminal phosphate between poly(P) and some nucleotide%2C but it is not clear which. [Central intermediary metabolism%2C Phosphorus compounds] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:11-222%2C Eval:1.7e-17%2C score:79.3],MGA_1358
