sequence11	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	91497	91805	.	-	0	ID=MGA_2149;product=type II toxin-antitoxin system RelB/DinJ family antitoxin;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005068595.1;translation=MRKTEVYQVRLDSQEKKQAFAVFKQLGITPAQAVRLFFKQVVLTKSIPFAIENQNINMEQLLKLRKAKASSLNQNASTLNEDDDHEDLFEELNALLGESDKT;locus_tag=LOCUS_21400;note=WP_005068595.1 type II toxin-antitoxin system RelB/DinJ family antitoxin (Acinetobacter) [pid:93.1%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.6e-46],Domain:cl01171:RelB RelB antitoxin. Plasmids may be maintained stably in bacterial populations through the action of addiction modules%2C in which a toxin and antidote are encoded in a cassette on the plasmid. In any daughter cell that lacks the plasmid%2C the toxin persists and is lethal after the antidote protein is depleted. Toxin/antitoxin pairs are also found on main chromosomes%2C and likely represent selfish DNA. Sequences in the seed for this alignment all were found adjacent to toxin genes. The resulting model appears to describe a narrower set of proteins than pfam04221%2C although many in the scope of this model are not obviously paired with toxin proteins. Several toxin/antitoxin pairs may occur in a single species. [Cellular processes%2C Toxin production and resistance%2C Mobile and extrachromosomal element functions%2C Other] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-49%2C Eval:1.2e-11%2C score:53.1%2C C-term missing],MGA_2149
