sequence12	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	55850	56860	.	+	0	ID=MGA_2229;product=allantoicase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_002121874.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_22200;gene=alc;EC_number=3.5.3.4;note=WP_002121874.1 allantoicase (Acinetobacter calcoaceticus/baumannii complex) [pid:95.2%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.5e-194],Domain:cl27253:Allantoicase Allantoicase repeat. Members of this family are the enzyme allantoicase (EC 3.5.3.4)%2C also called allantoate amidinohydrolase. This enzyme hydrolyzes allantoate to (S)-ureidoglycolate and urea%3B it can also degrade (R)-ureidoglycolate to glyoxylate and urea. Allantoinase (EC 3.5.2.5) hydrolyzes (S)-allantoin (a xanthine metabolite%2C via urate) to allantoate. Allantoate can then be degraded either by this enzyme%2C allantoicase%2C or by allantoate deiminase (EC 3.5.3.9). Members of the seed alignment for this model were taken from BRENDA. Proteins in this family contain two copies of the allantoicase repeat (pfam03561). A different but similarly named enzyme%2C allantoate amidohydrolase (EC 3.5.3.9)%2C simultaneously breaks down the urea to ammonia and carbon dioxide. [Purines%2C pyrimidines%2C nucleosides%2C and nucleotides%2C Other%2C Energy metabolism%2C Other] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:10-332%2C Eval:3.4e-167%2C score:466.2],MGA_2229
