sequence13	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	10704	11555	.	+	0	ID=MGA_2294;product=PHP domain-containing protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014207649.1;translation=MQGIDLHTHSNISDGTLSPELLVQAAVDVKLHTLALTDHDTMDGLQRAKNAAQPHDLQIISGVEISSQWSRPSTKKSYGVHIVALNMQDEAPILEALEQQKRIRAQRAEVICELLKKCIGFDIYQDVLDKVENQPDRITRTHIAKALVEKNVVSRPQQAFDRFLKEGKRAFVKFEGLGLKETIEVIHNSKGFAVLAHPTRYDLSATNTRYLIEIFASYGGDAVELPPPVDPLSTRQMIDRMIEQHHLAISIGSDFHGENMPWIKLGNTPKPASNQQGIWERFI;locus_tag=LOCUS_22840;note=WP_014207649.1 PHP domain-containing protein (Acinetobacter calcoaceticus/baumannii complex) [pid:88.0%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:7.9e-143],COG:COG0613:YciV Predicted metal-dependent phosphoesterase TrpH%2C contains PHP domain [Category:R%2C Aligned:1-260%2C Eval:7.4e-45%2C score:149.9],MGA_2294
sequence13	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	11563	12474	.	-	0	ID=MGA_2295;product=bestrophin family protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005064169.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_22850;note=WP_005064169.1 bestrophin family protein (Acinetobacter) [pid:96.7%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:7.4e-166],Domain:cl01544:Bestrophin Bestrophin%2C RFP-TM%2C chloride channel. Bestrophin is a 68-kDa basolateral plasma membrane protein expressed in retinal pigment epithelial cells (RPE). It is encoded by the VMD2 gene%2C which is mutated in Best macular dystrophy%2C a disease characterized by a depressed light peak in the electrooculogram. VMD2 encodes a 585-amino acid protein with an approximate mass of 68 kDa which has been designated bestrophin. Bestrophin shares homology with the Caenorhabditis elegans RFP gene family%2C named for the presence of a conserved arginine (R)%2C phenylalanine (F)%2C proline (P)%2C amino acid sequence motif. Bestrophin is a plasma membrane protein%2C localized to the basolateral surface of RPE cells consistent with a role for bestrophin in the generation or regulation of the EOG light peak. Bestrophin and other RFP family members represent a new class of chloride channels%2C indicating a direct role for bestrophin in generating the light peak. The VMD2 gene underlying Best disease was shown to represent the first human member of the RFP-TM protein family. More than 97%25 of the disease-causing mutations are located in the N-terminal RFP-TM domain implying important functional properties. The bestrophins are four-pass transmembrane chloride-channel proteins%2C and the RFP-TM or bestrophin domain extends from the N-terminus through approximately 350 amino acids and contains all of the TM domains as well as nearly all reported disease causing mutations. Interestingly%2C the RFP motif is not conserved evolutionarily back beyond Metazoa%2C neither is it in plant members. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-297%2C Eval:2.2e-86%2C score:258.5],MGA_2295
