sequence15	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	55959	56843	.	-	0	ID=MGA_2542;product=YbgF trimerization domain-containing protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014206981.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_25310;note=WP_014206981.1 YbgF trimerization domain-containing protein (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:76.2%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:1.8e-121],Domain:cl26250:TPR_6 Tetratricopeptide repeat. Members of this protein family are the product of one of seven genes regularly clustered in operons to encode the proteins of the tol-pal system%2C which is critical for maintaining the integrity of the bacterial outer membrane. The gene for this periplasmic protein has been designated orf2 and ybgF. All members of the seed alignment were from unique tol-pal gene regions from completed bacterial genomes. The architecture of this protein is a signal sequence%2C a low-complexity region usually rich in Asn and Gln%2C a well-conserved region with tandem repeats that resemble the tetratricopeptide (TPR) repeat%2C involved in protein-protein interaction. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:5-290%2C Eval:7.0e-28%2C score:105.6],MGA_2542
