sequence20	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	18176	19669	.	+	0	ID=MGA_2938;product=nicotinate phosphoribosyltransferase;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014206821.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_29230;EC_number=6.3.4.21;note=WP_014206821.1 nicotinate phosphoribosyltransferase (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:98.2%25%2C q_cov:100.0%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:2.0e-287],Domain:cl28369:PncB Nicotinic acid phosphoribosyltransferase [Coenzyme transport and metabolism]. A deep split separates two related families of proteins%2C one of which includes experimentally characterized examples of nicotinate phosphoribosyltransferase%2C an the first enzyme of NAD salvage biosynthesis. This model represents the other family. Members have a different (longer) spacing of several key motifs and have an additional C-terminal domain of up to 100 residues. One argument suggesting that this family represents the same enzyme is that no species has a member of both families. Another is that the gene encoding this protein is located near other NAD salvage biosynthesis genes in Nostoc and in at least four different Gram-positive bacteria. NAD and NADP are ubiquitous in life. Most members of this family are Gram-positive bacteria. An additional set of mutually closely related archaeal sequences score between the trusted and noise cutoffs. [Biosynthesis of cofactors%2C prosthetic groups%2C and carriers%2C Pyridine nucleotides] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:12-493%2C Eval:6.2e-34%2C score:129.3],MGA_2938
