sequence30	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	8010	8684	.	+	0	ID=MGA_3423;product=LrgB family protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_005804924.1;translation=MFMILYGFLITLVGYLCAKPLNRRFPQVPLLVFGMFIVIGLLSILKVPYEEYRLYVNDLFSHLLGYVTVALAIPLAAMRYDDLPLKSVIGILCFASISAVALPMGLAYLLHMSEPTILAFATRAVTTPIALNIATLLHAPETLVTLIVILSGVIGAAFSPFLLKHIHDERASGLALGLAAHAIGTAQAWQRGPVAGRYAAFGMALNGVFTAIWLPTFMLSFGIH;locus_tag=LOCUS_33980;note=WP_005804924.1 LrgB family protein (Acinetobacter) [pid:93.2%25%2C q_cov:99.1%25%2C s_cov:99.1%25%2C Eval:3.1e-114],Domain:cl00596:LrgB LrgB-like family. Members of this small but broadly distibuted (Gram-positive%2C Gram-negative%2C and Archaeal) family appear to have multiple transmembrane segments. The function is unknown. A homolog%2C LrgB of Staphylococcus aureus%2C in the same small superfamily but in an outgroup to this subfamily%2C is regulated by LytSR and is suggested to act as a murein hydrolase. Of the three paralogous proteins in B. subtilis%2C one is a full length member of this family%2C one lacks the C-terminal 60 residues and has an additional 128 N-terminal residues but branches within the family in a phylogenetic tree%2C and one is closely related to LrgB and part of the outgroup. [Hypothetical proteins%2C Conserved] [Superfamily%2C Aligned:1-215%2C Eval:1.7e-43%2C score:143.5],MGA_3423
