sequence34	MetaGeneAnnotator	CDS	291	1193	.	-	0	ID=MGA_3514;product=MaoC/PaaZ C-terminal domain-containing protein;inference=COORDINATES:ab initio prediction:MetaGeneAnnotator,similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_014207045.1;;locus_tag=LOCUS_34850;note=WP_014207045.1 MaoC/PaaZ C-terminal domain-containing protein (Acinetobacter pittii) [pid:98.2%25%2C q_cov:94.7%25%2C s_cov:100.0%25%2C Eval:2.0e-160],Domain:cl00509:hot_dog N/A. This is the dehydratase domain of polyketide synthases. Structural analysis shows these DH domains are double hotdogs in which the active site contains a histidine from the N-terminal hotdog and an aspartate from the C-terminal hotdog. Studies have uncovered that a substrate tunnel formed between the DH domains may be essential for loading substrates and unloading products. [Superfamily%2C Aligned:198-278%2C Eval:4.2e-07%2C score:45.9%2C C-term missing],MGA_3514
